t scale. A narrow payments account would be a meaningful shift because it separates settlement access from full bank privileges. If the Fed and regional Reserve Banks align on that model, more crypto-linked financial infrastructure could move closer to core dollar rails.\n\n**3. What signals should traders watch now?**\nWatch the 60-day comment process, the Fed's 120-day legal review, and any revisions to balance limits or eligibility language. Comments from bank trade groups matter because they will test how much political resistance the proposal faces. Traders should also watch whether firms with stablecoin or custody exposure are publicly preparing applications or adjusting charter strategies.\n\n**4. How does this affect Ripple stablecoin activity?**\nRipple has a strong reason to care because faster payment access could improve reserve movement and redemption logistics around RLUSD. The same logic applies to Circle and other stablecoin issuers that rely on smooth dollar settlement. A workable limited account would not solve every regulatory issue, but it could tighten the link between token issuance and the traditional payment system.\n\n**Sources:**\n- CoinDesk: https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/20/federal-reserve-proposes-limited-master-accounts-long-pursued-by-crypto-firms\n- Decrypt: https://decrypt.co/368431/trump-orders-fed-to-review-crypto-firms-access-to-master-accounts\n'''\n# validations\nassert '—' not in article\nassert article.count('### ') == structure['h3_count']\nassert article.count('**1.') == 1 and article.count('**2.') == 1 and article.count('**3.') == 1 and article.count('**4.') == 1\nassert article.count('https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/20/federal-reserve-proposes-limited-master-accounts-long-pursued-by-crypto-firms') == 2\nassert article.count('https://decrypt.co/368431/trump-orders-fed-to-review-crypto-firms-access-to-master-accounts') == 2\nbody_anchor_count = article.count('](')\nassert body_anchor_count == 2\nwc = len(re.findall(r\"\\b\\S+\\b\", article)) + 3  # for final numeric word count token replacing placeholder line added below\nfinal = article + f'\\n[Word Count: {wc}]\\n'\nwc_final = len(re.findall(r\"\\b\\S+\\b\", final))\n# align printed count with actual file count if tokenization differs\nif wc_final != wc:\n    final = article + f'\\n[Word Count: {wc_final}]\\n'\n    wc = wc_final\nassert structure['word_min'] <= wc <= structure['word_max'], wc\nassert final.splitlines()[0] == 'META'\nfor path in [run_dir/'article'/'raw.md', pathlib.Path('/tmp/crypto-article-raw.md')]:\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    path.write_text(final)\nprint(wc)\nPY"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1982,"output":4179,"cacheRead":14336,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20497,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779362045591,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DhvdlnZbzWviphFhDbOGWFRdqoAjM"}}
